<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Corfu Declaration</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1917</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Corfu Declaration was an agreement signed on 20 July 1917 on the Greek island of Corfu by the Serbian government in exile under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nikola-pasic">Nikola Pašić</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yugoslav-committee">Yugoslav Committee</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ante-trumbic">Ante Trumbić</a>. It proposed a single kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbs">Serbs</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croats">Croats</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovenes">Slovenes</a> under the Serbian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karadordevic-dynasty">Karađorđević dynasty</a>, with equal status for their names, flags, alphabets and religions, and became the basis of the kingdom proclaimed in 1918.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/corfu-declaration.jpg" alt="Corfu Declaration" width="320" height="504" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SCG Historical Archives · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Izjav1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
